#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:2
msgid "Custom Discovery Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:5
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:7
msgid ""
"This guide assumes that you have already set up Syncthing. If you haven't "
"yet, head over to :ref:`getting-started` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:11
msgid "Installing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:13
msgid ""
"Go to `releases <https://github.com/syncthing/discosrv/releases>`__ and "
"download the file appropriate for your operating system. Unpacking it will "
"yield a binary called ``discosrv`` (or ``discosrv.exe`` on Windows). Start "
"this in whatever way you are most comfortable with; double clicking should "
"work in any graphical environment. At first start, discosrv will generate "
"the directory ``/var/discosrv`` (``X:\\var\\discosrv`` on Windows, where X "
"is the partition ``discosrv.exe`` is executed from) with configuration. If "
"the user running ``discosrv`` doesn't have permission to do so, create the "
"directory and set the owner appropriately or use the command line switches "
"(see below) to select a different location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:25
msgid "Configuring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:28
msgid ""
"If you are running an instance of syncthing on the discovery server, you "
"must either add that instance to other nodes using a static address or bind "
"the discovery server and syncthing instances to different IP addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:33
msgid ""
"Running discosrv with non-default settings requires passing the respective "
"parameters to discosrv on every start. ``discosrv -help`` gives you all the "
"tweakables with their defaults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:39
msgid ""
"Usage of discosrv:\n"
"  -cert string\n"
"      Certificate file (default \"cert.pem\")\n"
"  -db-backend string\n"
"      Database backend to use (default \"ql\")\n"
"  -db-dsn string\n"
"      Database DSN (default \"memory://discosrv\")\n"
"  -debug\n"
"      Debug\n"
"  -http\n"
"      Listen on HTTP (behind an HTTPS proxy)\n"
"  -key string\n"
"      Key file (default \"key.pem\")\n"
"  -limit-avg int\n"
"      Allowed average package rate, per 10 s (default 5)\n"
"  -limit-burst int\n"
"      Allowed burst size, packets (default 20)\n"
"  -limit-cache int\n"
"      Limiter cache entries (default 10240)\n"
"  -listen string\n"
"      Listen address (default \":8443\")\n"
"  -stats-file string\n"
"      File to write periodic operation stats to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:64
msgid "Certificates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:66
msgid ""
"The discovery server provides service over HTTPS. To ensure secure "
"connections from clients there are three options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:69
msgid ""
"Use a CA-signed certificate pair for the domain name you will use for the "
"discovery server. This is like any other HTTPS website; clients will "
"authenticate the server based on it's certificate and domain name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:73
msgid ""
"Use any certificate pair and let clients authenticate the server based on "
"it's \"device ID\" (similar to Syncthing-to-Syncthing authentication). In "
"this case, using ``syncthing -generate`` is a good option to create a "
"certificate pair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:78
msgid ""
"Pass the ``-http`` flag if the discovery server is behind an SSL-secured "
"reverse proxy. See below for configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:81
msgid ""
"For the first two options, the discovery server must be given the paths to "
"the certificate and key at startup. This isn't necessary with the ``http`` "
"flag::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:84
msgid ""
"$ discosrv -cert /path/to/cert.pem -key /path/to/key.pem\n"
"Server device ID is 7DDRT7J-UICR4PM-PBIZYL3-MZOJ7X7-EX56JP6-IK6HHMW-S7EK32W-"
"G3EUPQA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:87
msgid ""
"The discovery server prints it's device ID at startup. In the case where you "
"are using a non CA signed certificate, this device ID (fingerprint) must be "
"given to the clients in the discovery server URL::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:91
msgid ""
"https://disco.example.com:8443/v2/?id=7DDRT7J-UICR4PM-PBIZYL3-MZOJ7X7-"
"EX56JP6-IK6HHMW-S7EK32W-G3EUPQA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:93
msgid "Otherwise, the URL (note the trailing slash after the ``v2``) will be::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:95
msgid "https://disco.example.com:8443/v2/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:98
msgid "Pointing Syncthing at Your Discovery Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:100
msgid ""
"By default, Syncthing uses a number of global discovery servers, signified "
"by the entry ``default`` in the list of discovery servers. To make Syncthing "
"use your own instance of discosrv, open up Syncthing's web GUI. Go to "
"settings, Global Discovery Server and add discosrv's host address to the "
"comma-separated list, e.g. ``https://disco.example.com:8443/v2/``. Note that "
"discosrv uses port 8443 by default. For discosrv to be available over the "
"internet with a dynamic IP address, you will need a dynamic DNS service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:108
msgid ""
"If you wish to use *only* your own discovery server, remove the ``default`` "
"entry from the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:112
msgid "Reverse Proxy Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:114
msgid ""
"The discovery server can be run behind an SSL-secured reverse proxy. This "
"allows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:117
msgid ""
"Use of a subdomain name without requiring a port number added to the URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:118
msgid "Sharing an SSL certificate with multiple services on the same server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:121
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:123
msgid "Run the discovery server using the -http flag  :code:`discosrv -http`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:124
msgid "SSL certificate/key configured for the reverse proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:125
msgid ""
"The \"X-Forwarded-For\" http header must be passed through with the client's "
"real IP address"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:127
msgid ""
"The \"X-SSL-Cert\" must be passed through with the PEM-encoded client SSL "
"certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:129
msgid ""
"The proxy must request the client SSL certificate but not require it to be "
"signed by a trusted CA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:133
msgid "Nginx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:135
msgid ""
"These three lines in the configuration take care of the last three "
"requirements listed above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:138
msgid ""
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-SSL-Cert $ssl_client_cert;\n"
"ssl_verify_client optional_no_ca;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:144
msgid ""
"The following is a complete example Nginx configuration file. With this "
"setup, clients can use https://discovery.mydomain.com as the discovery "
"server URL in the Syncthing settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/discosrv.rst:148
msgid ""
"# HTTP 1.1 support\n"
"proxy_http_version 1.1;\n"
"proxy_buffering off;\n"
"proxy_set_header Host $http_host;\n"
"proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n"
"proxy_set_header Connection $proxy_connection;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $proxy_x_forwarded_proto;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-SSL-Cert $ssl_client_cert;\n"
"upstream discovery.mydomain.com {\n"
"    # Local IP address:port for discovery server\n"
"    server 172.17.0.6:8443;\n"
"}\n"
"server {\n"
"        server_name discovery.mydomain.com;\n"
"        listen 80;\n"
"        access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log vhost;\n"
"        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;\n"
"}\n"
"server {\n"
"        server_name discovery.mydomain.com;\n"
"        listen 443 ssl http2;\n"
"        access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log vhost;\n"
"        ssl_protocols TLSv1 TLSv1.1 TLSv1.2;\n"
"        ssl_ciphers ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-"
"SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384: DHE-RSA-"
"AES128-GCM-SHA256:DHE-DSS-AES128-GCM-SHA256:kEDH+AESGCM:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-"
"SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-SHA:E CDHE-ECDSA-AES128-"
"SHA:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-SHA384:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-SHA:"
"ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-SHA:DHE-RSA-AES128-SHA25 6:DHE-RSA-AES128-SHA:DHE-DSS-"
"AES128-SHA256:DHE-RSA-AES256-SHA256:DHE-DSS-AES256-SHA:DHE-RSA-AES256-SHA:"
"AES128-GCM-SHA256:AES256-GCM-SHA3 84:AES128-SHA256:AES256-SHA256:AES128-SHA:"
"AES256-SHA:AES:CAMELLIA:DES-CBC3-SHA:!aNULL:!eNULL:!EXPORT:!DES:!RC4:!MD5:!"
"PSK:!aECDH:!EDH-DSS -DES-CBC3-SHA:!EDH-RSA-DES-CBC3-SHA:!KRB5-DES-CBC3-SHA;\n"
"        ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;\n"
"        ssl_session_timeout 5m;\n"
"        ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:50m;\n"
"        ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/certs/discovery.mydomain.com.crt;\n"
"        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/certs/discovery.mydomain.com.key;\n"
"        ssl_dhparam /etc/nginx/certs/discovery.mydomain.com.dhparam.pem;\n"
"        add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000\";\n"
"        ssl_verify_client optional_no_ca;\n"
"        location / {\n"
"                proxy_pass http://discovery.mydomain.com;\n"
"        }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

